# Frappe Python Patterns

## DocType Controllers

```python
# ✅ Standard DocType controller structure
class MyDocType(Document):
    def validate(self):
        self.validate_required_fields()

    def before_submit(self):
        self.set_status()

    def on_submit(self):
        self.update_related_docs()
```

## Database Operations

```python
# ❌ BAD - raw SQL
frappe.db.sql("SELECT name FROM tabItem WHERE item_code = %s", item_code)

# ✅ GOOD - use frappe ORM and Query Builder (https://docs.frappe.io/framework/user/en/api/query-builder)
frappe.get_value("Item", {"item_code": item_code}, "name")
frappe.get_list("Item", filters={"item_code": item_code}, pluck="name")
customers = frappe.qb.DocType('Customer')
q = (
 frappe.qb.from_(customers)
 .select(customers.id, customers.fname,customers.lname, customers.phone)
 .where((customers.fname == 'Max') | (customers.id.like('RA%')) )
 .where(customers.lname == 'Mustermann')
)

python

```

## Whitelist APIs

```python
@frappe.whitelist()
def get_production_data(work_order: str) -> dict:
    """Return production data for a work order."""
    frappe.has_permission("Work Order", "read", throw=True)
    return frappe.get_doc("Work Order", work_order).as_dict()
```

## Error Handling

- Use `frappe.throw()` for validation errors (rolls back transaction)
- Use `frappe.msgprint()` for warnings/info
- Log errors with `frappe.log_error()`
